---
// Start-here picks are specific posts the user asked for by name, not an
// auto-generated pick per category.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactBlock from '../components/ContactBlock.astro';
import headerPhoto from '../header_final.jpeg';

const allPosts = await getCollection('posts');
const startHereSlugs = [
  'touloused-confused-my-coup-de-coeur-restaurants',
  'my-first-month-in-toulouse',
  'ello-and-au-revoir-a-year-s-tapif-recap',
];
const startHere = startHereSlugs
  .map((slug) => allPosts.find((p) => p.data.slug === slug))
  .filter((p) => p !== undefined);

const facts = [
  { label: 'Currently in', value: 'Toulouse (7 years and counting!)' },
  { label: 'Always ordering', value: 'the second glass (& planche mixte)' },
  { label: 'My ideal weekend', value: 'Pyrenees or brunch, no in-between' },
  { label: 'Most American habit', value: 'iced coffee in January' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="About · Fork Spoon & Straw" description="American, in Toulouse." mastheadVariant="default">
  <section class="about-hero">
    <div class="hero-top">
      <h1 class="about-greeting">Bonjour,<br />c&rsquo;est <em>lele</em>.</h1>
      <Image class="portrait" src={headerPhoto} alt="" width={800} height={1067} />
    </div>
    <p class="about-copy">
      I grew up in Los Angeles, where a great meal could be anything from Mom&rsquo;s cooking to a
      street taco in a parking lot (IYKYK). I thought I had the whole food thing figured out. Then
      in January 2017, I stepped off a plane in Paris for a semester abroad and realized the
      French don&rsquo;t just eat well - they build their entire day around it. My whole world
      split into &ldquo;before France&rdquo; and &ldquo;after France.&rdquo;
    </p>
    <p class="about-copy">
      I went to Skidmore College in upstate New York, where I double majored in Health &amp;
      Exercise Science and French. Yes, both. No, I can&rsquo;t explain it either (unless you know
      me, and then it makes total sense). I spent most of college quietly plotting how to get back
      to France after my semester abroad. It worked!
    </p>
    <p class="about-copy">
      After graduating in 2018, I landed in the Alps near Nice teaching English to high schoolers.
      Sounds romantic, <em>non</em>? The reality was one <em>brasserie</em>, a ski lift, and a
      social life that revolved entirely around both for two days a week. But the mountains
      (and <em>la mer</em>) were incredible, the <em>raclette</em> was endless, and I was once
      again hooked.
    </p>
    <p class="about-copy">
      In September of 2019, I took a plane (and a leap of faith!) across the Atlantic to Toulouse
      for a job in Communications and Marketing - but let&rsquo;s be real, I was also here for
      the <em>terrasses</em>, the Garonne at golden hour, and the fact that people here are very
      serious about <em>apéro</em>.
    </p>
    <p class="about-copy">
      Seven years later? Still here in <em>la vie rose</em>. Still discovering
      new <em>pépites</em> around every corner and still showing up to the <em>marché</em> on a
      sunny Sunday and leaving with way more produce than one person needs. These days
      you&rsquo;ll find me cycling through the Pyrenees, standing in front of a cheese counter
      pretending to choose between two <em>tommes</em> when really I&rsquo;m panicking about all
      six, or bopping around adding new restaurants to my never-ending list of things to try.
    </p>
    <p class="about-copy">
      This is where I keep all of it - the plates that made me go <em>miam</em>, the trips that
      turned into stories, the recipes I actually make at home, and the reality of building a life
      where you dream in franglais, accidentally say &ldquo;du coup&rdquo; in English, and need at
      least three pieces of paper you didn&rsquo;t know existed every time you deal with
      the <em>préfecture</em>.
    </p>
    <p class="about-copy"><em>Bienvenue</em> - grab a glass, I&rsquo;m glad you&rsquo;re here!</p>
    <p class="about-signoff">xx lele</p>
  </section>

  <div class="fact-list">
    {
      facts.map((f) => (
        <div class="fact-row">
          <span>{f.label}</span>
          <span class="fact-value">{f.value}</span>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <div class="start-here-wrap">
    <div class="start-here">
      <span class="start-label">Start here</span>
      <h2 class="start-title">Three posts that explain the whole thing</h2>
      <div class="start-links">
        {
          startHere.map((post, i) => (
            <a href={`/posts/${post.data.slug}`}>
              {i + 1} &nbsp; {post.data.title}
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ContactBlock />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Full-bleed creme "paper" behind the capped text column -- see the same
     trick on PostLayout's .post; otherwise this reads as a narrow island
     floating in the sand background on wide desktops. */
  .about-hero {
    position: relative;
    padding: var(--sp-22) var(--gutter-text) var(--sp-20);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .about-hero::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 50%;
    width: 100vw;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    background: var(--creme);
    z-index: -1;
  }

  .about-greeting {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    font-size: 40px;
    line-height: 0.98;
    color: var(--espresso);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-greeting em {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: var(--paprika);
  }

  .hero-top {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .portrait {
    width: 100%;
    height: 330px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 50% 30%;
  }

  .about-copy {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.68;
    color: var(--cacao);
  }

  .about-copy em {
    color: var(--paprika);
  }

  .about-signoff {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 28px;
    color: var(--paprika);
    margin-top: var(--sp-8);
  }

  .fact-list {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0 var(--gutter-text) var(--sp-20);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .fact-list::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 50%;
    width: 100vw;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    background: var(--creme);
    z-index: -1;
  }

  .fact-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: 14px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-roquefort);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 15px;
    color: #3d3833;
  }

  .fact-row:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-roquefort);
  }

  .fact-value {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--roquefort-ink);
  }

  .start-here-wrap {
    padding: var(--sp-20) var(--gutter-card) var(--sp-22);
  }

  .start-here {
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    background: var(--creme);
    border: 1px solid var(--fleur-de-sel);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--saumon);
    padding: var(--sp-20);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-10);
  }

  .start-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--paprika);
  }

  .start-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--espresso);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .start-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 9px;
    padding-top: var(--sp-4);
  }

  .start-links a {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--roquefort-ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .about-hero,
    .fact-list {
      max-width: var(--measure);
      margin-inline: auto;
      padding-inline: 0;
    }

    .start-here-wrap {
      max-width: var(--measure);
      margin-inline: auto;
      padding-inline: 0;
    }

    /* Photo sits beside the greeting instead of its own full-width row. */
    .hero-top {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 32px;
    }

    .about-greeting {
      flex: 1;
      font-size: 56px;
    }

    /* Matches the source's own 3:4 ratio so cover has nothing awkward to
       crop -- just smaller now that it sits next to the greeting. */
    .portrait {
      width: 240px;
      height: 320px;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
